{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01027",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 6.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.74,
      "end_seconds": 12.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "great hello, come in and and sit down how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.05,
      "end_seconds": 27.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps. Um, doctor, it's shaking chills and a high temperature. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.77,
      "end_seconds": 34.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "so, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.56,
      "end_seconds": 38.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "it's been three weeks now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.72,
      "end_seconds": 48.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.45,
      "end_seconds": 56.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "I get some relief from blankets. Honestly, a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.01,
      "end_seconds": 61.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Okay have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.81,
      "end_seconds": 68.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a racing heart as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.13,
      "end_seconds": 75.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 75.75,
      "end_seconds": 81.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.6,
      "end_seconds": 90.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The The racing heart? That's been for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.65,
      "end_seconds": 100.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.26,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.84,
      "end_seconds": 105.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Mild really honestly on and off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.15,
      "end_seconds": 114.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Right, right. Have you had shaking chills and a high temperature before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.56,
      "end_seconds": 123.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 124.58,
      "end_seconds": 132.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 91, temperature is 38.1 degrees, pressure 118 over 66."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.7,
      "end_seconds": 134.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.77,
      "end_seconds": 139.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.5,
      "end_seconds": 143.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.19,
      "end_seconds": 159.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "You are hot your heart is racing and your blood pressure is low which worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.4,
      "end_seconds": 163.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "okay that's enough for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.79,
      "end_seconds": 178.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Okay, have you noticed rash, stiff neck or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.47,
      "end_seconds": 191.38,
      "duration_seconds": 11.91,
      "text": "no no rash no stiff neck no chest pain i was feeling confused at one point but that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.56,
      "end_seconds": 194.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.1,
      "end_seconds": 198.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.82,
      "end_seconds": 201.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.57,
      "end_seconds": 204.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.76,
      "end_seconds": 209.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.31,
      "end_seconds": 213.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "actually, my grandmother had dementia"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.03,
      "end_seconds": 217.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "and and alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.09,
      "end_seconds": 223.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.23,
      "end_seconds": 226.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.02,
      "end_seconds": 232.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.74,
      "end_seconds": 234.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.76,
      "end_seconds": 237.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.34,
      "end_seconds": 241.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.77,
      "end_seconds": 258.86,
      "duration_seconds": 16.09,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux, yes. I, I have asthma, for about ten years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.12,
      "end_seconds": 260.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "mm-hmm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.58,
      "end_seconds": 265.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "I have anxiety for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.54,
      "end_seconds": 268.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.2,
      "end_seconds": 287.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "What do you take on a a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.79,
      "end_seconds": 297.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called it's a round yellow one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.56,
      "end_seconds": 302.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.11,
      "end_seconds": 317.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "For the anxiety, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I'd been on Seretide inhaler, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.82,
      "end_seconds": 323.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.17,
      "end_seconds": 338.95,
      "duration_seconds": 13.78,
      "text": "hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.3,
      "end_seconds": 354.62,
      "duration_seconds": 14.32,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. It's hard to say. Possible sepsis needing urgent treatment is one possibility and a severe urine or chest infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.49,
      "end_seconds": 358.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Is it dangerous doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.56,
      "end_seconds": 376.73,
      "duration_seconds": 17.17,
      "text": "I understand the the worry. At the moment I'd say it's possible sepsis needing urgent treatment, and we'll know more once the lactate and blood tests is back. I'm going to order lactate and blood tests, for sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 377.32,
      "end_seconds": 379.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "the earliest is Thursday, 2 pm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.53,
      "end_seconds": 414.6,
      "duration_seconds": 33.07,
      "text": "I'll request a chest X-ray, it'll help with fever. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'll request blood cultures, it'll help with fever with low blood pressure. I want to admit you to hospital now for fluids and antibiotics. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. We'll refer you to the emergency team. Do get help quickly if you cannot be brought in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.69,
      "end_seconds": 417.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "we'll catch up straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.09,
      "end_seconds": 421.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Yes you know that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.92,
      "end_seconds": 424.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "does all of that that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.52,
      "end_seconds": 429.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "No that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}